<title>UK: Elf says awarded deepwater oil permit in Congo. [corrected 09:03 gmt]</title>
<headline>Elf says awarded deepwater oil permit in Congo. [corrected 09:03 gmt]</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>French oil major Elf Aquitaine on Tuesday said it was awarded a new exploration license in deep waters off the Republic of Congo (Corrects from Democractic Republic of Congo, clarifying not formerly Zaire).</p>
<p>Elf Congo becomes the operator in a production sharing contract of Congo's Very Deep Sea South license and expected to associate other partners.</p>
<p>The permit covers 5,070 square kilometres and is located in depths of between 2,000-3,000 meters.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 6280</p>
